  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "105-108 is one unit (the reciter joins 105-106-107-108). Paradise and Hell are never drawn: night for the Fire, light for Paradise, geometric for «إن ربك فعال لما يريد», a light plate for «عطاء غير مجذوذ»; no fire, river or gold. «إلا ما شاء ربك» (107:7-10, 108:12-15) is not glossed: the tafsirs differ (Al-Muyassar: the sinful monotheists; As-Sa'di: the time before entering). The plan's «الشقي والسعيد» was the verse's own pair. STAGING v4: All of 105-108 stays ambient: the Day (no soul speaks except by His permission), the Fire and Paradise are the unseen and are never drawn: no people, no crowd, no fire, river, gold or jewel. c1 (105, geometric): a two-paths plate for the wretched and the happy (105:8-10); params.quiet over 105:1-7 (His permission). c2 (106-107, night_sky, no light mood over the Fire): no plate over the Fire; geometric for your Lord does what He wills (107:11-15); params.quiet over all of 106-107 (no pulse over the Fire, the exception of His will and His names). c3 (108, light): Paradise is not pictured; a light plate for a gift never cut off (108:16-18, starting on the gift, not on a word for Allah); params.quiet over the exception of His will (108:12-15). 107:7-10 and 108:12-15 stay unglossed (the tafsirs differ). Cover: the two-paths plate (the two destinies)."
